---
description: Application Hang (EID 1002) → OCSF Application Error (6008, General Error)
args:
  positional:
    - name: windows
      description: The Windows event to map.
      type: field
    - name: ocsf
      description: The field that receives the OCSF event.
      type: field
---

// Windows closed or suspended an application that stopped responding. The
// event does not say who closed it: the user, or Windows, for example when it
// suspends an app (HangType Quiesce). The reporting process and the System
// account in the header are those of Windows Error Reporting. Process Activity
// requires an actor, so the hang maps to Application Error, as Windows Error
// Reporting (1001) does. That class has no process object, so the hung
// process (AppName, AppVersion, ProcessId, StartTime, ExeFileName) stays in
// unmapped, together with TerminationTime, ReportId, PackageFullName, and
// PackageRelativeAppId. HangType, such as Quiesce, details the error.
@name = "ocsf.application_error"

$ocsf.category_uid = 6
$ocsf.class_uid = 6008
$ocsf.activity_id = 1  // General Error
$ocsf.type_uid = $ocsf.class_uid * 100 + $ocsf.activity_id

$ocsf.severity_id = 3  // Medium — Windows Event Log Level 2 (Error)

$ocsf.status_detail = move $windows.EventData.HangType?
